{"at": "2026-11-24T07:05:07Z", "class": ["software"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-b89990889bc1"], "id": "45833deef0dfe825", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "rework", "text": "Before delegating to helpers in isolated worktrees, commit and check which branch the worktree is cut from: the harness cut them from main, which held only the first commit, so two helpers found an empty project. Creating the worktrees by hand from HEAD (git worktree add --detach) and copying node_modules fixed it.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T07:05:16Z", "class": ["software"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-8955cf705048", "review:sha256-3774d979b6b1"], "id": "8bd3c77a60be374a", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "rework", "text": "Test a connected service with one small write before promising a deploy on it: the Vercel connection answered reads but refused the file upload (403, no permission to create). A built web app can instead be published as a private page with its bundle as a supporting file, which the owner opens on his phone.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T07:05:16Z", "class": ["software"], "evidence": ["gate:checks", "review:sha256-b74d27790c41"], "id": "38d733a04fc76050", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "first-success", "text": "For a visual choice among many options, render every option on the same scenes and publish one page with two views (by option, and by scene across all options) and a full-screen viewer that flips between options on the same scene. Look at contact sheets of every image before publishing: that pass found a staging bug, a cropped subject and a white-chested black cat.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T07:05:26Z", "class": ["software"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "f77f9315308540e2", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "first-success", "text": "A cloud session with no graphics chip can still render and look at real-time 3D: headless Chromium draws WebGL2 in software. Render many shots from one page load (rebuilding the scene for every shot cost five times more), and shrink the shadow map first when frames are slow (a third of the size made clip frames about four times faster).", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T07:05:26Z", "class": ["software"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "2c66a8fd20c69c79", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "rework", "text": "When a project is set up, make git ignore the folder where the harness keeps helper worktrees: adding every file otherwise commits those worktrees as embedded repositories, which then have to be removed in a second commit.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T08:31:12Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "9ca722edfea078c6", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "first-success", "text": "When the owner answers a menu of looks with 'something between A, B and C', build the blend at once on the same sample scenes as a per-surface mix, send a handful of pictures in chat within minutes, and let his next sentence refine it. Three quick rounds of this settled an art style that a ten-option menu had not.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T08:31:20Z", "class": ["owner"], "evidence": ["gate:checks", "owner:turn@2026-11-24T07:26:47.331Z#f9316965a46d"], "id": "0ffdd61c525c8370", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "owner-correction", "text": "The owner reverses strong instructions after seeing results: 'no layers at all' became 'I like the layers but less pronounced'. Build such choices as a dial with a number, not as a rewrite, and treat the newest sentence as the rule while keeping the earlier one in the ledger as dropped, with the reason.", "trust": "owner-stated"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T08:31:20Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "f798415ab3bdf04b", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "rework", "text": "A privately published page only serves known file types: a raw binary data file is refused. Ship a numeric grid as a lossless picture (two bytes of each value in two colour channels) and decode it on a canvas with colour conversion and alpha premultiplication switched off; check once that it decodes to identical values.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-24T08:31:20Z", "class": ["method"], "evidence": ["gate:checks"], "id": "341000faa275d22f", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "837acef2-1dc7-583e-888f-4f0c9456db1d", "signal": "first-success", "text": "A look where some things are drawn (pen line, hatching) and the rest is solid can be had in two steps instead of a full deferred pipeline: the one scene pass writes a second image with surface direction, kind of thing and light, and one screen pass inks edges and hatches only where the kind says drawn.", "trust": "observed"}
